WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.235
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.838
you know
from her work in "Black-ish."

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.773
Her holiday movie,
"Candy Cane Lane,"

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.408
is streaming now on Prime Video.

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.610
She also stars
in "American Fiction,"

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.878
which opens in select theaters
December 15th

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:13.847
and nationwide in January.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.980
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.450
our friend Tracee Ellis Ross,
everybody!

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.586
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:39.338 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:41.274
-Hello.
-You look fantastic,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:43.043
and it's very important to me
that you look fantastic.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.344
-Why is that?
-Because I'm coming up

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:48.748
on a milestone birthday that
you passed last year.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:50.917
-Oh, I'm so deep
in the 50s now. I'm 51.

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:53.619
-Yeah.
-I can tell you all about it.

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:55.354
-Are you loving it?
-I love it so much.

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:56.689
-Oh, that's great.
-I love it so much.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.558
I have to say,
I've always loved getting older,

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.661
but there's something
really spectacular

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:02.862
about getting to an age

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.597
where you feel really
comfortable saying "no."

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.866
You feel comfortable
just sort of going,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.034
"Yeah, that
doesn't really work for me."

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.702
Or, "You know what?
I'm not feeling that."

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.804
Or, "Yeah, I want to do that."

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.137
-That's great.
Everything you just said,

00:01:12.137 --> 00:01:15.842
I'm so excited to try on my wife
and have not work.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.311
-Maybe it works
because I'm single.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.046
-It's still good.
-It feels really good.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.448
I'm glad to have you
feel so enthusiastic about it.

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.582
-Yeah, I mean,
there's some things

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.652
that are absolutely
odd, weird, and strange.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.152
Like sometimes when you wake up
in the morning,

00:01:27.152 --> 00:01:31.057
you're like, did I sleep or did
somebody beat me up? Not sure.

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.859
-Because you're just,
that deep soreness.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.394
-You get out of bed
and you're like, [ Groans ].

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.063
Sometimes if I ended up
sleeping on my stomach

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.832
and I turn over, I'm like, "Oh,
God, I think I'm paralyzed."

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.568
And then --
-The worst about that is,

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:42.735
yeah, when you do that
and somebody's like,

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.170
"Oh, were you working out?"

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.939
And you're like, "No."
-"Not at all."

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.440
No, I slept.
-Slept weird.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.241
-Had a good night's sleep.
Sorry. Let me just move my hair.

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:51.844
Okay. Go ahead.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:53.746
-Alright, well, I'll look out
for all of those things.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.114
-And are you going to have
a big celebration?

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.248
Everybody does different things.

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:57.884
I actually did something big
for my birthday.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:59.919
-You did, huh?
-It was pretty special.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.220
Speeches and the whole thing.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:02.488
I might as well have been
a wedding.

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:04.290
-See, that's wonderful.
-It was nice.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.324
-See, I'm not going to do that.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.625
-No?

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:07.927
But everybody
has a different version.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.395
-My problem is just
where it falls.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.064
It's December 28th,
so it's like,

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.232
nobody is ready for a party.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:14.033
-You're a December 28th baby?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.869
-That is tough.
-It's the worst.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.537
I feel like because
of where it landed,

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.506
they should only count
every other one,

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.441
and I'm about to be 25.

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:23.877
-I'm game.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.545
I think during the pandemic,
none of those years happened.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.046
-Yeah, right?
-No, I'm actually 48.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.080
-Yeah, there you go.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.115
-Yeah.
-Well, then

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.183
we don't even have to
worry about

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.083
that big birthday
for a couple of years.

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:32.152
Doesn't matter.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.219
-You have time
to work on your speeches.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.354
-I'm gonna have another one.

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:37.824
-Now, you did a holiday movie?

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.892
-I did a holiday movie.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.593
-And you have
a big family yourself.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.694
-I do.
-And are the holidays...

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.262
-There's five kids.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:46.298
They're all married with kids
and just grandbabies

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:47.667
and just uncles and aunts

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.101
and just people
running all over each other.

00:02:49.101 --> 00:02:50.703
-Do you love the chaos?
-I do.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.838
-Okay, and you always have?
-I always have.

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:55.908
And then I have somehow
created this very serene,

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.944
quiet life for myself,
so I go into the chaos,

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.314
and then I come out into
my little, quiet world, yeah.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.816
-Do you serve a very
valuable purpose as someone

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.619
who maybe has energy reserves
that the parents don't have?

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.388
-Well,
the most important purpose

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.855
that I serve with my family,

00:03:09.855 --> 00:03:11.257
to the point that I'm not going
home for Christmas this year

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.725
and my mom literally was like,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.361
"But who's going
to make the salads?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.896
No, we're going to miss you,

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.064
but who's going
to make the salads?"

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.232
-So your mother, Diana Ross,

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:21.867
doesn't have
a backup salad person?

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:23.969
-No, it's me.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:26.505
We sat together for a second,
really thinking, like,

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.741
"Would Ross make the salads?
Would Evan?"

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.909
No, no one makes the salad.
I make the salads."

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.379
-Wow. You're gonna
have to FedEx salads.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:34.814
-I'm usually in charge of food
when I'm home.

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.516
-God, they really
take advantage of you.

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:39.118
-Well, everyone else
has kids running around.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.118
-Yeah, yeah, that's true.
-I'm like,

00:03:40.118 --> 00:03:41.954
yeah, so I do salads.

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.856
-You did this film --

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.092
-I cook food too,
but I'm particularly good

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.526
with the salads.

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.029
I'm sorry.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.231
-I love that you're like,
"I'm a bit of a chef."

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.867
"What do you do?"
-"Salads."

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.037
-You did this
holiday movie with Eddie Murphy.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.372
-Eddie Murphy!
-That's amazing.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.640
-Yes!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.441
[ Cheering ]

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.343
-I mean, three months
with Eddie Murphy.

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:07.313
-Three months, and we had a ball
and did not exhaust

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.581
all the stories
that had to be told.

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:10.316
And we would go tit for tat.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:13.052
We would just keep trying to see
who could do a better story.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.320
And it was a ball.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:16.154
-So you've lived
a fascinating life,

00:04:16.154 --> 00:04:18.190
that you're willing to go
tit for tat with Eddie Murphy.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.925
-I was like, "Get me in here,
get me in here.

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.028
Oh, yeah, you? Oh, yeah, really?
Oh, Stevie Wonder?

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.296
Oh, let me tell you
about Stevie Wonder."

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.064
-Oh, that's real good.
-It was really good.

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.365
-That's real good.
-It was really good.

00:04:26.365 --> 00:04:27.633
-Had you met him before?
-No.

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:29.068
-Okay, wow.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.736
-Bizarre, never met him.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.705
First day of work,
my first day of work,

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.108
I'm like, "Okay, well,
I'm going to meet Eddie Murphy."

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.742
-Yeah.
-So he's like a cat.

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:39.278
He's very quiet.
You don't know he's coming.

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.680
So he kind of walked up to me
and he said,

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.048
"Tracee Ellis Ross?"

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:44.684
And I was like, okay,
we're bowing, alright.

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.685
I was like, "Eddie Murphy."

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:48.187
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:50.022
And then I sat and I asked him,
I was like, "Are there things

00:04:50.022 --> 00:04:51.457
that you need, like,
that I need to know?

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.127
Like, am I allowed to talk
while you're acting? Can I...?"

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.360
He was like,
"What are you talking about?"

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:56.229
And I was like, "Well,
I've worked with actors

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.363
where, you know, you can't."

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.231
And then I said,
"And how do I address you?

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:02.602
Do I call you Eddie, Mr.
Schmurphy? What's the scoop?"

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.169
And he was like, "Eddie."
And I said, "Great."

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:05.871
And then we were
just off to the races.

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:07.440
That's fantastic.
-It was really good.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.041
-Do you feel
like you're a little tired

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.242
of the holidays
because you had to pretend it

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:11.510
was Christmas for three months?

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:12.544
-It's not because of the movie.

00:05:12.544 --> 00:05:15.280
-Okay.
-Yeah.

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:18.684
-No, I love the holiday season,

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.453
but I also am a person
who doesn't do a tree.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:21.720
-Yeah.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:22.755
-Because then
you have to take it down, so...

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.423
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.423 --> 00:05:26.025
-Tell me about it.
-I mean, get it organized.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.894
-That's what I say

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:29.462
every year when they put up that
30 Rock tree.

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.396
I'm like,
"What are you guys doing?"

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:31.797
-Guys, then got to take it down.

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.066
What are you doing?
-You think this part's hard?

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.800
-Pshh.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.535
Taking down the tree
is so hard.

00:05:36.535 --> 00:05:38.404
-Imagine that one!
-Oh, my God.

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.038
-The dumbest thing in the world.

00:05:40.038 --> 00:05:43.676
-Do not sign me up.
-Do not sign me up!

00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:44.977
I have a lot more
to ask you about,

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:46.612
because you have
a lot of projects right now.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.082
Tracee Ellis Ross, we'll
be right back after this.

